WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:00.931 --> 00:02.132 align:center line:81%
Sisters and brothers,

00:02.833 --> 00:06.570 align:center line:79%
thank you for your faithful devotion
in coming unto Jesus Christ

00:06.570 --> 00:08.205 align:center line:81%
during these challenging times.

00:08.839 --> 00:11.441 align:center line:81%
You are wonderful, you are beautiful;

00:11.808 --> 00:13.610 align:center line:81%
you are each a child of God.

00:14.311 --> 00:19.016 align:center line:79%
It is my prayer that we recognize the
influence of the Holy Ghost as we become,

00:19.249 --> 00:22.486 align:center line:79%
and help one another
become, true disciples,

00:22.853 --> 00:26.857 align:center line:79%
or truly devoted disciples
of Jesus Christ, and feel of his joy

00:26.857 --> 00:29.192 align:center line:81%
as we worship in the house of the Lord.

00:29.192 --> 00:31.361 align:center line:81%
President Russell M Nelson declared:

00:31.728 --> 00:36.333 align:center line:79%
“Now is the time for you and for me to
prepare for the Second Coming of our Lord

00:36.333 --> 00:38.135 align:center line:81%
and Savior, Jesus the Christ.

00:38.502 --> 00:43.040 align:center line:79%
Now is the time for us to make
our discipleship our highest priority.

00:43.574 --> 00:46.643 align:center line:79%
In a world filled with
dizzying distractions.

00:46.643 --> 00:50.514 align:center line:79%
how can we do this?”
President Nelson provided the answer:

00:50.781 --> 00:53.717 align:center line:79%
“Regular worship
in the temple will help us.

00:54.151 --> 00:56.920 align:center line:79%
In the house of the Lord,
we focus on Jesus Christ. ...

00:56.920 --> 00:59.890 align:center line:79%
We come to know Him. ...
Every sincere seeker

00:59.890 --> 01:02.593 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ
will find him in the temple.”

01:03.527 --> 01:07.564 align:center line:79%
So, how do we become, and help one
another become, devoted disciples

01:07.564 --> 01:12.035 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ? We minister
to the one. Ministering

01:12.035 --> 01:16.807 align:center line:79%
in the Savior's way involves love
without judgment, compassion, kindness,

01:16.807 --> 01:19.643 align:center line:81%
and patience. As we minister to the one,

01:19.643 --> 01:24.247 align:center line:79%
we invite the one to come unto Christ
and to worship in the house of the Lord

01:24.448 --> 01:26.917 align:center line:81%
to receive of His redeeming power.

01:28.285 --> 01:32.723 align:center line:79%
In other words, we help one another
become devoted disciples as we minister

01:32.723 --> 01:36.393 align:center line:79%
to the one in ways that lead
to the house of the Lord.

01:37.194 --> 01:41.565 align:center line:79%
We learn from Jesus Christ the power
of ministering to the one with love

01:41.765 --> 01:42.866 align:center line:81%
and without judgment.

01:43.433 --> 01:46.336 align:center line:79%
You remember the Samaritan
woman at the well.

01:46.903 --> 01:51.942 align:center line:79%
This woman may have felt unimportant,
alone, discouraged, and unseen.

01:52.376 --> 01:54.344 align:center line:81%
She may have felt she did not belong.

01:54.711 --> 01:57.047 align:center line:79%
Throughout her life,
she had five husbands

01:57.047 --> 02:00.550 align:center line:79%
and the man who she was living
with was not her husband.

02:01.051 --> 02:04.187 align:center line:79%
Others may have imposed
unrighteous judgment without knowing

02:04.187 --> 02:05.656 align:center line:81%
her life’s circumstances.

02:05.922 --> 02:10.761 align:center line:79%
This may be one of the reasons she came
to the well alone in the hottest part

02:10.761 --> 02:14.064 align:center line:79%
of the day. And yet,
she was one of the first

02:14.064 --> 02:17.401 align:center line:79%
to whom Jesus Christ
declared He was the Messiah.

02:18.101 --> 02:21.371 align:center line:81%
To Him, this woman was a daughter of God.

02:21.905 --> 02:26.443 align:center line:79%
Jesus taught that woman that through
Him one can receive eternal life,

02:26.443 --> 02:29.046 align:center line:79%
partaking of the living
water. He declared,

02:29.046 --> 02:32.816 align:center line:79%
“Whosoever drinketh of the water
that I shall give... shall never thirst;

02:32.816 --> 02:35.285 align:center line:79%
but the water that I shall give ...
shall be ... a well of water

02:35.285 --> 02:37.187 align:center line:81%
springing up to everlasting life.”

02:37.821 --> 02:41.058 align:center line:79%
The woman of Samaria
felt the Savior’s love

02:41.391 --> 02:45.195 align:center line:79%
and received the witness through
the Spirit that He is the Messiah.

02:45.762 --> 02:50.834 align:center line:79%
After this witness, she returned to the
city, invited others to come and see,

02:51.168 --> 02:55.038 align:center line:79%
and many believed Jesus “is indeed
the Christ, the Savior of the world.”

02:55.439 --> 02:59.242 align:center line:79%
Christ ministered to the one
with love; and as a result,

02:59.476 --> 03:02.245 align:center line:81%
others became His devoted disciples.

03:02.879 --> 03:05.882 align:center line:79%
We learn of the power
of ministering to the one with compassion

03:05.882 --> 03:08.051 align:center line:81%
from Christ’s Apostles Peter and John.

03:08.652 --> 03:11.955 align:center line:79%
You remember a certain man,
lame from birth,

03:11.955 --> 03:15.158 align:center line:79%
laid daily at the gate
of the temple asking for money.

03:15.158 --> 03:21.531 align:center line:79%
This man may have felt unimportant,
alone, discouraged, and unseen.

03:21.965 --> 03:24.301 align:center line:81%
He may have felt he did not belong.

03:24.968 --> 03:29.473 align:center line:79%
“Then Peter said, silver and gold
have I none; but such as I have

03:29.473 --> 03:33.243 align:center line:79%
[I] give [unto] thee: In the name
of Jesus Christ of Nazareth

03:33.310 --> 03:38.615 align:center line:79%
rise up and walk.” Peter took the man
by his right hand, lifted him up,

03:38.749 --> 03:42.719 align:center line:79%
and the man was made whole.
Immediately following the miracle,

03:42.986 --> 03:48.725 align:center line:79%
the man entered into the temple
with Peter and John, “walking,

03:48.859 --> 03:51.161 align:center line:81%
and leaping, and praising God.”

03:51.795 --> 03:56.700 align:center line:79%
Peter and John ministered to the one
in ways that led to the house of the Lord,

03:56.867 --> 04:00.237 align:center line:79%
and this man became
Christ's devoted disciple.

04:01.471 --> 04:03.807 align:center line:81%
My friends, there has been moments

04:03.807 --> 04:07.310 align:center line:79%
in my life where I too
have felt unimportant,

04:07.310 --> 04:10.480 align:center line:81%
alone, discouraged, and unseen.

04:11.314 --> 04:13.917 align:center line:81%
I have felt as if I did not belong.

04:14.584 --> 04:16.520 align:center line:81%
I was baptized and confirmed a member

04:16.520 --> 04:19.289 align:center line:79%
of The Church of Jesus Christ
of Latter-day Saints when I was 19

04:19.289 --> 04:21.124 align:center line:81%
years old. One year later,

04:21.124 --> 04:24.027 align:center line:79%
I accepted a call to serve
as a full-time missionary.

04:24.027 --> 04:27.764 align:center line:79%
But there was much I had not
yet learned about Church history.

04:27.764 --> 04:29.499 align:center line:81%
Early in my missionary service,

04:29.699 --> 04:32.269 align:center line:79%
I learned that there was a period
that those of Black African

04:32.269 --> 04:35.939 align:center line:79%
descent were not allowed to enjoy all
of the blessings of worshipping

04:35.939 --> 04:37.707 align:center line:81%
in the house of the Lord.

04:37.707 --> 04:44.414 align:center line:79%
Learning this for the first time brought
feelings of anger, confusion, doubt,

04:44.414 --> 04:46.616 align:center line:81%
and fear. These feelings were

04:46.616 --> 04:51.655 align:center line:79%
so intense that my ability to recognize
the Holy Ghost was lost for a season.

04:52.189 --> 04:55.725 align:center line:79%
Fortunately, I had a wonderful
missionary companion, Kevin Vick,

04:56.226 --> 04:59.462 align:center line:79%
who ministered to me with love,
patience, and kindness.

04:59.896 --> 05:03.500 align:center line:79%
Each night as he witnessed my feelings
of doubt and uncertainty,

05:03.500 --> 05:07.804 align:center line:79%
he would simply say to the younger
Elder Johnson, “I love you.”

05:08.672 --> 05:13.043 align:center line:79%
After about two weeks,
I allowed myself to feel of Kevin's love.

05:13.510 --> 05:17.414 align:center line:79%
I gained the courage to pray to Heavenly
Father in the name of Jesus Christ.

05:17.414 --> 05:22.018 align:center line:79%
And as I prayed, I was drawn to section
6 of the Doctrine and Covenants,

05:22.052 --> 05:28.258 align:center line:79%
verses 21–24, which states: “Behold,
I am Jesus Christ, the Son of God. ...

05:28.658 --> 05:30.861 align:center line:79%
I am the light which
shineth in darkness. ...

05:31.027 --> 05:34.698 align:center line:79%
cast your mind upon the night
that you cried unto me in your heart,

05:34.698 --> 05:38.702 align:center line:79%
that you might know concerning the
truth of these things. ... Did I not speak

05:38.702 --> 05:40.871 align:center line:81%
peace to your mind concerning the matter?

05:41.271 --> 05:44.608 align:center line:79%
What greater witness
can you have than from God?”

05:45.442 --> 05:47.844 align:center line:81%
As I read, I remembered.

05:48.378 --> 05:50.881 align:center line:79%
I remembered the day that I
had fasted and prayed to know

05:50.881 --> 05:53.884 align:center line:79%
that the Book of Mormon
is the word of God,

05:53.884 --> 05:57.454 align:center line:79%
and that Joseph Smith is the prophet
of the Restoration.

05:57.821 --> 06:01.157 align:center line:79%
I remembered covenants made
in the house of the Lord that connect me

06:01.157 --> 06:04.394 align:center line:79%
to Jesus Christ in such
a personal and intimate way.

06:04.394 --> 06:07.731 align:center line:81%
I felt of the Savior’s love, His mercy,

06:07.931 --> 06:10.567 align:center line:79%
and of His assurance
that The Church of Jesus Christ

06:10.567 --> 06:14.371 align:center line:79%
of Latter-day Saints is His
kingdom upon the earth

06:14.471 --> 06:18.174 align:center line:79%
and is necessary to prepare us
for His Second Coming.

06:18.808 --> 06:20.377 align:center line:81%
Because I remembered,

06:20.777 --> 06:23.113 align:center line:79%
I again was able
to recognize the Holy Ghost

06:23.113 --> 06:29.452 align:center line:79%
and to understand more fully that Jesus
is the Christ, and I am His disciple.

06:30.253 --> 06:36.726 align:center line:79%
At times we will have unanswered questions
and feelings of being unimportant,

06:37.127 --> 06:39.996 align:center line:81%
discouraged, alone, and unseen;

06:40.530 --> 06:45.068 align:center line:79%
however, my friends, we must press forward
with faith in Jesus Christ

06:45.068 --> 06:47.304 align:center line:81%
and remember His words:

06:48.271 --> 06:50.073 align:center line:81%
“Let not your heart be troubled.”

06:50.340 --> 06:54.844 align:center line:79%
“In the world ye shall have tribulation:
but be of good cheer;

06:55.211 --> 06:57.547 align:center line:81%
I have overcome the world.”

06:58.081 --> 07:02.919 align:center line:79%
I am a witness to this reality
and of the Savior's promised blessing.

07:03.887 --> 07:07.958 align:center line:79%
So, what can we do to ensure
our ministering to the one

07:07.958 --> 07:10.760 align:center line:81%
in the Savior's way is most effective?

07:11.394 --> 07:14.431 align:center line:79%
Living the doctrine
of Christ will help us.

07:14.831 --> 07:17.968 align:center line:79%
Living the doctrine of Christ
as President Nelson described,

07:17.968 --> 07:21.037 align:center line:79%
“can produce the most powerful,
virtuous cycle,

07:21.037 --> 07:26.009 align:center line:79%
creating spiritual momentum in our lives
as we strive to live the higher laws

07:26.009 --> 07:30.246 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ, ... the Savior
lifts us up above the pull

07:30.246 --> 07:35.085 align:center line:79%
of this fallen world by blessing us
with greater to charity, humility,

07:35.151 --> 07:39.823 align:center line:79%
generosity, kindness,
self-discipline, peace, and rest.”

07:40.323 --> 07:45.128 align:center line:79%
This spiritual momentum produced
by living the doctrine of Christ,

07:45.495 --> 07:50.166 align:center line:79%
Elder Dale G. Renlund explains,
“not only powers the transformation

07:50.166 --> 07:53.069 align:center line:79%
of our divine nature
into our eternal destiny

07:53.336 --> 07:58.541 align:center line:79%
but also motivates us to help [to
minister to] others in appropriate ways.”

07:58.975 --> 08:01.444 align:center line:81%
Elder Renlund reminds us that “the

08:01.444 --> 08:05.482 align:center line:79%
Savior’s job is to heal,
[to make us whole].

08:05.982 --> 08:11.287 align:center line:79%
Our job is to love ... and [to] minister
in such a way that others are drawn

08:11.287 --> 08:12.455 align:center line:81%
to Jesus Christ.”

08:13.490 --> 08:19.162 align:center line:79%
Our ability to live the doctrine
of Christ will be enhanced by daily study

08:19.162 --> 08:22.599 align:center line:79%
of the Book of Mormon and weekly
partaking of the sacrament.

08:22.932 --> 08:26.603 align:center line:79%
President Nelson declared that the Book
of Mormon “teaches the doctrine

08:26.603 --> 08:28.905 align:center line:79%
of Christ ... [and] provides
the [most] fullest

08:28.905 --> 08:32.208 align:center line:79%
and most [clearest] understanding
of the Atonement of Jesus Christ

08:32.208 --> 08:34.511 align:center line:81%
to be found anywhere.”

08:36.246 --> 08:38.681 align:center line:81%
I love this book,

08:40.350 --> 08:43.253 align:center line:81%
and prayerfully partaking of the ordinance

08:43.253 --> 08:47.524 align:center line:79%
of the sacrament each week will increase
our understanding of the Atonement

08:47.557 --> 08:51.528 align:center line:79%
of Jesus Christ and provide
spiritual renewal, comfort,

08:51.528 --> 08:53.797 align:center line:81%
and the power of godliness in our lives.

08:54.397 --> 08:57.801 align:center line:79%
Remember, “in the ordinances
[of the priesthood]

08:58.201 --> 09:00.804 align:center line:81%
the power of godliness is manifest”

09:00.804 --> 09:05.275 align:center line:79%
and this power, which comes from
Jesus Christ, strengthens our desire

09:05.408 --> 09:08.211 align:center line:81%
and our ability to minister to the one.

09:09.012 --> 09:11.281 align:center line:81%
My study of the Book of Mormon

09:11.648 --> 09:16.052 align:center line:79%
and partaking of the sacrament
minimizes feelings of discouragement,

09:16.519 --> 09:21.591 align:center line:79%
escalates my determination to minister
to the one in the Savior's way,

09:21.991 --> 09:25.829 align:center line:79%
and helps make discipleship
my highest priority.

09:26.729 --> 09:32.102 align:center line:79%
My friends, I promise that as we live
the doctrine of Christ

09:32.102 --> 09:35.805 align:center line:79%
and minister to the one in ways that lead
to the house of the Lord,

09:36.206 --> 09:39.609 align:center line:79%
we will press forward
with faith in Jesus Christ

09:39.642 --> 09:45.715 align:center line:79%
even amid unanswered questions
and feelings of being unimportant, alone,

09:45.748 --> 09:47.584 align:center line:81%
discouraged, and unseen.

09:47.984 --> 09:50.753 align:center line:79%
We will invite the one
to come unto Jesus Christ

09:50.753 --> 09:52.922 align:center line:81%
and to worship in the house of the Lord,

09:52.922 --> 09:58.628 align:center line:79%
to receive of His redeeming power
and love. In the house of the Lord,

09:58.828 --> 10:01.197 align:center line:81%
we will “feel [the Savior’s] mercy.

10:01.798 --> 10:05.068 align:center line:79%
[We] will find answers
to [our] most vexing questions.

10:05.301 --> 10:09.239 align:center line:79%
[And we] will better
comprehend the joy of His gospel.”

10:09.706 --> 10:12.408 align:center line:81%
In the name of Jesus Christ,

10:12.709 --> 10:14.310 align:center line:81%
amen.

